  "notes": "Bad Boy vocal quartet across Stevie J / Hitmen productions and Tim & Bob ballads, 1996–2003. The research gives \"78–102 straight; ballads 64–88\" with five sourced key/tempo pairs, so the straight band 78–102 is the base with the mode at 98 and `halfTime` false. The three drum deltas are quoted: \"kick on 1 and the 16th before 3\" moves the secondary anchor to `2a`; \"clap on 2&4 for the uptempos\" is a clap stack; \"16th hats with a shuffled feel on the Hitmen cuts\" is why `swing.amount` sits at 0.58 with a continuous 16th lane rather than the parent's heavier 0.62. Harmony is \"two-chord minor-9th vamps and IV–V turnarounds\", encoded as two-chord minor families plus a IV–V family, with the ninth share raised well above the parent's; the major keys the entry names are why the major families carry real weight. \"Guitar lick countermelody\" is the counter at +12 with `answer_lick` leading; \"phrases end with a group unison hit\" is `endVariation` off and a moderate density. The low end is \"plucked synth bass with short portamento into the root\" and on one record \"the bass and kick are effectively one voice\" — hence `mirror_kick` with a real `glideProb`, and no `bass808` block. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are all velocity and density numbers, the swing figure and the melody register; the research gives instrumentation and tempo, not a kit.",
